<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  folio-assistant — authoring a document end to end (no Lean, no required TeX).

  Source of truth: this file. Open it in bpmn.io, Camunda Modeler, or any other
  BPMN 2.0 tool. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated from it
  by `bun run cat render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG.

  The shape is deliberately the paper process minus the Lean lane and plus one
  step: `5 · Check the profile`. That step is what lets everything downstream
  run without a Lean toolchain or a TeX installation, because it is what keeps
  a document folio from quietly acquiring content that would need them.

  The <bootstrap.processes:skill> extension on an activity names the folio-assistant skill
  that implements it; <cat-harness.processes:bean> marks a step that reads or writes the shared
  work plan in beans/.
-->
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:bootstrap.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns#"
                  xmlns:cat-harness.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/processes/ns#"
                  id="Definitions_DocumentAuthoring"
                  targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows"
                  exporter="folio-assistant" exporterVersion="1">
  <bpmn:import namespace="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns#" location="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns.jsonld" importType="http://www.w3.org/ns/json-ld"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="author" name="Author"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="authoring-agent" name="Authoring agent"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="authoring-committee" name="Authoring Committee"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="build-pipeline" name="Build pipeline"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="reviewer" name="Reviewer / SME"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="work-plan" name="Work plan (beans)"/>

  <bpmn:import namespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows" location="contributor-feedback.bpmn" importType="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" />
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_DocumentAuthoring">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_DocumentAuthoring" name="Authoring a document — plan to published" processRef="Process_DocumentAuthoring" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_DocumentAuthoring" name="Authoring a document" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>
      How a document folio — structured prose and policy guidance, with no Lean and no required TeX — is authored, built and reviewed end to end. folio-assistant — authoring a document end to end (no Lean, no required TeX).
      Source of truth: this file. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated
      from it by `bun run cat render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG.
      The shape is the paper process minus the Lean lane and plus one step, the profile
      check, which is what keeps a document folio publishable without either toolchain.
    </bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <cat-harness.processes:policy enforcement="advisory" />
    </bpmn:extensionElements>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="Process_DocumentAuthoring_LaneSet">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Author" name="Author (person)" partitionElementRef="author">
        <bpmn:documentation>The only place a person acts before the process becomes agent- and pipeline-driven: Task_Plan sets the chapters, the blocks each needs and which statements are normative, once, before Lane_WorkPlan seeds a bean and Lane_Agent takes over every later edit, including every iteration the review and profile-check loops send back.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>StartEvent_NewDocument</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Plan</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_WorkPlan" name="Work plan — beans (shared by humans and agents)" partitionElementRef="work-plan">
        <bpmn:documentation>Touched exactly once in this process — Task_SeedPlan turns the plan into a bean right after Task_Plan, so a resumed session or a sibling agent can pick the authoring loop up without re-deriving what was decided at the top.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_SeedPlan</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_BeanOpen</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_BeanYours</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_BeanNotYours</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Agent" name="Authoring agent (system)" partitionElementRef="authoring-agent">
        <bpmn:documentation>Task_AuthorBlocks is where every loop in this process lands — a profile violation from Lane_Build and an iterate from Lane_Reviewer both come back here — so this lane, not either gate, is what actually turns a rejection into a fixed block; Task_Scaffold runs once, before either loop exists.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Scaffold</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_AuthorBlocks</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Build" name="Build pipeline — validate · render · publish" partitionElementRef="build-pipeline">
        <bpmn:documentation>Owns the one gate this process has that the paper process does not — the profile check — so nothing with a math kind, a lean field or a .lean sibling reaches Task_Validate or Task_Render pretending to be document content; everything downstream of Gateway_ProfileClean assumes that profile.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ProfileCheck</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_ProfileClean</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Validate</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Render</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Publish</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_Published</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_BeanClose</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Reviewer" name="Reviewer / subject-matter expert" partitionElementRef="reviewer">
        <bpmn:documentation>Owns the one gate that decides publish or iterate, and is deliberately unspecialised: this process relaxes the paper process's clinical-SME lane into whichever reviewer a given document actually binds, because no single expertise fits every document the way it does a guideline.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Review</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_ReviewOutcome</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Committee" name="Authoring Committee" partitionElementRef="authoring-committee">
        <bpmn:documentation>The people writing the document with the editor. While it is a working draft they give feedback through the Contributor Feedback sheet, one change set per row, and each row runs Process_ContributorFeedback.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_ContributorFeedback</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="StartEvent_NewDocument" name="New document">
      <bpmn:outgoing>D01</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:userTask id="Task_Plan" name="1 · Plan the document">
      <bpmn:documentation>Scope it: chapters, the blocks each needs, which statements are normative.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="content-plan" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>D01</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>D02</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Task_SeedPlan" name="2 · Seed the work plan&#10;[todo-manager]" calledElement="GT_SeedWorkPlan">
      <bpmn:outgoing>D03</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_1</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Scaffold" name="3 · Scaffold the folio&#10;[folio_init]">
      <bpmn:documentation>folio_init writes content/, uploads/, library/, the manifests, the builder shim and AGENTS.md. Skipped when the folio already exists.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="document-structure" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>D03</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>D04</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_AuthorBlocks" name="4 · Author blocks">
      <bpmn:documentation>Every block edit runs the HCI validation gate — see editing-hci-validation.bpmn. A normative statement is a `recommendation` block (bean 55ao), drafted through normative-statements: one statement per block, a folio-chosen label, and its strength as a code in a declared code list, so a reviewer signs off each one individually.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="document-authoring" />
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="normative-statements" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>D04</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>D07</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>D12</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>D05</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_ProfileCheck" name="5 · Check the profile">
      <bpmn:documentation>content_profile_check: no math kind, no lean field, no .lean sibling. This is the step a paper folio does not have, and the reason a document folio never needs Lean or TeX to publish.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="content-validate" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>D05</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>D06</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_ProfileClean" name="Within the declared profile?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Answered by the profile check (step 5): does every block stay within the folio's declared content profile? `violations` sends the author back to step 4 to fix the blocks; `clean` goes on to validation.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>D06</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>D07</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>D08</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Validate" name="6 · Validate">
      <bpmn:documentation>Schema and constraint checks over every block.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="content-validate" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>D08</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>D16</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>D09</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Render" name="7 · Render MD / HTML / PDF">
      <bpmn:documentation>Assemble to Markdown, then pandoc. The PDF goes through an HTML engine — never latexmk.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="document-publishing" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>D09</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>D10</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:userTask id="Task_Review" name="8 · Review and feedback">
      <bpmn:documentation>The reviewer this folio binds. authoring-document relaxes the base SME step precisely because no single lane fits every document.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="content-review" />
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="staging-review" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>D10</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>D11</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_ReviewOutcome" name="Ready to publish?">
      <bpmn:documentation>The reviewer's call after step 8. `iterate` returns to authoring with the feedback; `Authoring Committee feedback` sends a working draft to the committee through the Contributor Feedback sheet (Process_ContributorFeedback), and comes back to validation once its changes are merged; `approved` goes to publish.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>D11</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>D12</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>D13</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>D15</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Publish" name="9 · Publish">
      <bpmn:documentation>See draft-to-publication.bpmn for the review and release path this expands into. Release authorisation is not relaxable.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="content-publish" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>D13</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>D14</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_Published" name="Document published">
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_4</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_BeanOpen" name="Open the bean" calledElement="Process_BeanOpen">
      <bpmn:documentation>Process_BeanOpen: check before you create, find out whose the bean is, and claim it — or leave it alone when it is someone else's. The one place a claim is drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); the gateway after this reads which end it reached.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="bean-coordination"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>D02</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_BeanYours" name="Bean claimed?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads which end Process_BeanOpen reached. `claimed`: the bean is in progress and this process works it. `not yours`: a sibling session or a human holds it, nothing was written to it, and this process stops here rather than work a bean it does not own (bean-coordination).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_1</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_BeanNotYours" name="Not yours —&#10;left alone">
      <bpmn:documentation>Someone else holds the bean; this run stops without touching it.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_3</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_BeanClose" name="Close the bean" calledElement="Process_BeanClose">
      <bpmn:documentation>Process_BeanClose: end the bean in a state that says why — complete and archive it, scrap it with its reasons and archive it, or record the blocker and hand it back. The one place resolve and archive are drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); placed straight before the end so the engine's resolve sees nothing left but the archive step.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="todo-manager"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>D14</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_ContributorFeedback" name="Contributor feedback" calledElement="Process_ContributorFeedback">
      <bpmn:documentation>Process_ContributorFeedback: while the document is a working draft, the Authoring Committee gives feedback through the Contributor Feedback sheet, and each change set is edited and merged in its own pull request. When its changes are merged, the document is validated and rendered again (owner, 2026-10-31).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="review-sheet-script"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>D15</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>D16</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="D01" sourceRef="StartEvent_NewDocument" targetRef="Task_Plan" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="D02" sourceRef="Task_Plan" targetRef="Call_BeanOpen" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="D03" sourceRef="Task_SeedPlan" targetRef="Task_Scaffold" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="D04" sourceRef="Task_Scaffold" targetRef="Task_AuthorBlocks" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="D05" sourceRef="Task_AuthorBlocks" targetRef="Task_ProfileCheck" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="D06" sourceRef="Task_ProfileCheck" targetRef="Gateway_ProfileClean" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="D07" name="violations" sourceRef="Gateway_ProfileClean" targetRef="Task_AuthorBlocks" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="D08" name="clean" sourceRef="Gateway_ProfileClean" targetRef="Task_Validate" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="D09" sourceRef="Task_Validate" targetRef="Task_Render" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="D10" sourceRef="Task_Render" targetRef="Task_Review" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="D11" sourceRef="Task_Review" targetRef="Gateway_ReviewOutcome" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="D12" name="iterate" sourceRef="Gateway_ReviewOutcome" targetRef="Task_AuthorBlocks" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="D13" name="approved" sourceRef="Gateway_ReviewOutcome" targetRef="Task_Publish" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="D14" sourceRef="Task_Publish" targetRef="Call_BeanClose" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="D15" name="Authoring Committee feedback" sourceRef="Gateway_ReviewOutcome" targetRef="Call_ContributorFeedback" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="D16" sourceRef="Call_ContributorFeedback" targetRef="Task_Validate" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Bean_1" name="claimed" sourceRef="GW_BeanYours" targetRef="Task_SeedPlan"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Bean_2" sourceRef="Call_BeanOpen" targetRef="GW_BeanYours"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Bean_3" name="not yours" sourceRef="GW_BeanYours" targetRef="End_BeanNotYours"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Bean_4" sourceRef="Call_BeanClose" targetRef="EndEvent_Published"/>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_1">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_1" bpmnElement="Collaboration_DocumentAuthoring">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Participant_DocumentAuthoring_di" bpmnElement="Participant_DocumentAuthoring" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1390" height="885" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_Author_di" bpmnElement="Lane_Author" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="190" y="80" width="1360" height="125" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_WorkPlan_di" bpmnElement="Lane_WorkPlan" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="190" y="205" width="1360" height="200" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_Agent_di" bpmnElement="Lane_Agent" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="190" y="405" width="1360" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_Build_di" bpmnElement="Lane_Build" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="190" y="525" width="1360" height="180" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_Reviewer_di" bpmnElement="Lane_Reviewer" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="190" y="705" width="1360" height="130" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_Committee_di" bpmnElement="Lane_Committee" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="190" y="835" width="1360" height="130" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="StartEvent_NewDocument_di" bpmnElement="StartEvent_NewDocument">
        <dc:Bounds x="237" y="117" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="220" y="157" width="70" height="40" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Plan_di" bpmnElement="Task_Plan">
        <dc:Bounds x="295" y="90" width="120" height="90" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Call_BeanOpen_di" bpmnElement="Call_BeanOpen">
        <dc:Bounds x="295" y="293" width="120" height="90" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="GW_BeanYours_di" bpmnElement="GW_BeanYours" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="430" y="313" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="425" y="368" width="60" height="40" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="End_BeanNotYours_di" bpmnElement="End_BeanNotYours">
        <dc:Bounds x="437" y="227" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="477" y="227" width="100" height="36" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_SeedPlan_di" bpmnElement="Task_SeedPlan">
        <dc:Bounds x="525" y="283" width="120" height="110" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Scaffold_di" bpmnElement="Task_Scaffold">
        <dc:Bounds x="525" y="420" width="120" height="90" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_AuthorBlocks_di" bpmnElement="Task_AuthorBlocks">
        <dc:Bounds x="670" y="420" width="120" height="90" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_ProfileCheck_di" bpmnElement="Task_ProfileCheck">
        <dc:Bounds x="670" y="570" width="120" height="90" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gateway_ProfileClean_di" bpmnElement="Gateway_ProfileClean" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="813" y="590" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="788" y="644" width="100" height="40" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Validate_di" bpmnElement="Task_Validate">
        <dc:Bounds x="885" y="570" width="120" height="90" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Call_ContributorFeedback_di" bpmnElement="Call_ContributorFeedback">
        <dc:Bounds x="885" y="845" width="120" height="110" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Render_di" bpmnElement="Task_Render">
        <dc:Bounds x="1032" y="570" width="120" height="90" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Review_di" bpmnElement="Task_Review">
        <dc:Bounds x="1032" y="725" width="120" height="90" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gateway_ReviewOutcome_di" bpmnElement="Gateway_ReviewOutcome" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="1215" y="745" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1269" y="799" width="90" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Publish_di" bpmnElement="Task_Publish">
        <dc:Bounds x="1180" y="570" width="120" height="90" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Call_BeanClose_di" bpmnElement="Call_BeanClose">
        <dc:Bounds x="1330" y="570" width="120" height="90" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="EndEvent_Published_di" bpmnElement="EndEvent_Published">
        <dc:Bounds x="1475" y="597" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="1448" y="637" width="90" height="40" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="D01_di" bpmnElement="D01">
        <di:waypoint x="273" y="135" />
        <di:waypoint x="295" y="135" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
